.TH "ELEBAKE" "8" "September 2, 2026" "elebake" "System Manager\(cqs Manual"
.SH NAME
elebake \- compiler for a verified\-boot trust chain: build, sign,
attest, deploy, and the tamper\-detection loader\(cqs decisions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]elebake\f[R] \f[I]command\f[R] [\f[I]args\f[R] \&...]
.PP
\f[B]elebake help\f[R] [\f[I]command\f[R] | \f[I]group\f[R] |
\f[I]topic\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]elebake\f[R] maintains the trust chain of a locally built FreeBSD
boot loader: checked\-out source, measured expectations, Authenticode
signature, OpenPGP\-attested manifest, deployment to removable boot
media, and tamper witnesses read back at boot.
Detection, not enforcement: the design assumes the boot medium
\f[I]can\f[R] be tampered with and concentrates on noticing.
.PP
Every \f[B]elebake\f[R] command is a \f[I]generator\f[R]: it emits shell
text describing an action.
Whether that text is displayed, piped, or executed is decided by an
\f[I]interpreter\f[R] the operator controls per function (see
ENVIRONMENT).
The shipped default displays (\f[CR]cat\f[R]): inspect first, then pin
an executing interpreter.
Batch commands emit an unconditional sequence of further
\f[B]elebake\f[R] commands; checking is itself a command in the
sequence, and the batch machinery stops at the first failure.
.PP
The command reference below is generated from the tool\(cqs own help
corpus and is therefore always current; \f[CR]elebake help\f[R] renders
the same corpus in the terminal.
.SH THE FREEBSD SOURCES
\f[B]elebake\f[R] is nothing without the loader it compiles for.
The measurement, claim, gate and policy engine that reads the compiled
decisions at boot is a FreeBSD patch series \(en \f[I]platform trust
gates\f[R] \(en and the catalogs \f[B]elebake\f[R] offers
(\f[CR]stage measure\f[R], \f[CR]stage action\f[R],
\f[CR]stage when\f[R], \f[CR]stage phase show\f[R]) are parsed from the
headers of that series.
Against a stock FreeBSD tree the catalogs are empty and no foundation
can be built.
.PP
Get the tree that carries the series:
.IP
.EX
git clone \-b platform\-trust\-gates\-15.1 \(rs
    https://github.com/johannes\-bruegmann/freebsd\-src.git \(ti/git/freebsd\-src
elebake setenv ELEBAKE_FREEBSD_SRC \(ti/git/freebsd\-src
elebake freebsd prerequisites
.EE
.PP
The branch is based on releng/15.1 (15.1\-RELEASE); the loader\-side
engine lives under \f[CR]stand/efi/loader/local/\f[R] and its README
points back at this project.
Parts of the series are on their way upstream.
\f[CR]stage checkout\f[R] adds a git worktree of that repository per
stage, so the source stays one repository and every stage builds from a
named ref.
