transitive chain (gate, claims, expectations, triggers, whens, actions)
against the checkout\(cqs catalog, then appends; 4\-arg form inserts at
a 1\-based position
.TP
\f[B]stage phase policy drop <stage> <phase> <policy>\f[R]
Unbind a policy from a stage\(cqs phase (the policy itself survives)
.TP
\f[B]stage foundation check <stage>\f[R]
Sharp re\-verification of every bound phase right before emission:
phases still in the enum, every policy chain complete and in the
checkout\(cqs catalog (the world may have drifted)
.TP
\f[B]stage foundation make <stage>\f[R]
Generate foundation.c from the bound policies into the worktree
(generated\-only file; check first \(em this terminal renders what the
records say)
.TP
\f[B]stage foundation report <stage>\f[R]
Summarize the foundation of a stage: bound phases, their policies, the
referenced gates/claims and the emission target
.TP
\f[B]stage foundation <stage>\f[R]
The foundation batch: check stage \-> foundation check \-> foundation
make \-> foundation report
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All configuration lives in \f[CR]ELEBAKE_*\f[R] variables, layered as
\f[CR].env/local\f[R] (override, written by \f[CR]setenv\f[R]),
\f[CR].env/default\f[R] (the installed profile) and the shipped
templates.
Interpreter pins \f[CR]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_<function>\f[R] decide per
function whether emitted shell is displayed or executed: arity\-specific
before arity\-agnostic before the class default
(\f[CR]ELEBAKE_TERMINAL_INTERPRETER\f[R], default \f[CR]cat\f[R]).
Every variable answers \f[CR]elebake help env <VAR>\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_ARCHIVE_ATTEST_KEY\f[R]
The openpgp record that signs what this database exports \(en and the
signer a receiver expects
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_FREEBSD_PREREQUISITES\f[R]
Curated tool list \f[CR]freebsd prerequisites\f[R] probes at generation
time
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_FREEBSD_SRC\f[R]
Path to the FreeBSD source repository the stages build from
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INCLUDES\f[R]
Modules preloaded at startup (engine.sh is always loaded first)
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_attest\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]attest\f[R] \(en produces <file>.asc
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_attest_verify\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]attest verify\f[R] \(en the pinned signature check
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_filter_minimized\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]filter minimized\f[R] \(en writes the rescue
collection
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_help_manual\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]help manual\f[R] \(en Pandoc Markdown on stdout
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_incoming_clear\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]incoming clear\f[R] \(en empties import\(cqs
scratch directory
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_manifest\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]manifest\f[R] \(en writes the MANIFEST file
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_manifest_verify\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]manifest verify\f[R] \(en signature and hashes
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_provenance_add\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]provenance add\f[R] \(en files the receipt of an
import
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_provenance_collect\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]provenance collect\f[R] \(en receipt files for an
archive
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_provenance_dump\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]provenance dump\f[R] \(en dump TEXT
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_provenance_import\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]provenance import\f[R] \(en restore base element
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_provenance_list\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]provenance list\f[R] \(en the lineage, readable
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_provenance_serial\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]provenance serial\f[R] \(en advances export/serial
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_seal\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]seal\f[R] \(en appends the bundle hash to the dump
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_seal_verify\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]seal verify\f[R] \(en dump names THIS bundle?
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_stage_backup4\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]stage backup\f[R] (the arity\-4 act terminal ONLY)
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_stage_backup_list\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]stage backup list\f[R] \(en the rollback decision
view
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_stage_rollback_apply\f[R]
Interpreter for \f[CR]stage rollback apply\f[R] \(en the write onto the
medium
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/db\f[R]
the active database (symlink)
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/.env/{local,default}/\f[R]
the layered variable store: overrides (\f[CR]setenv\f[R]) over the
installed profile over the shipped templates
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/.log/YYYY\-MM\-DD/\f[R]
per\-invocation traces \(en the debugging ground truth
(\f[CR]elebake last\f[R])
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/stage/<stage>/\f[R]
a stage record: \f[CR]boot/\f[R] (the built tree),
\f[CR]backup/<medium>/<label>/\f[R] (backup records), \f[CR]media/\f[R],
\f[CR]marker/\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/provenance/\f[R]
receipts of every admitted import (the lineage)
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/worktree/\f[R]
git worktrees of the FreeBSD source; build trees live outside the
database
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/bundle/\f[R], \f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/incoming/\f[R]
where an exported bundle is handed to the user, and import\(cqs scratch
area
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a database, connect the sources, register keys, build and publish
a stage:
.IP
.EX
\&./elebake.sh bootstrap current minimal | sh
\&./elebake.sh setenv ELEBAKE_FREEBSD_SRC \(ti/git/freebsd\-src
\&./elebake.sh pkcs11 add db \(aqpkcs11:token=...;object=db\(aq /root/sb/db.crt
\&./elebake.sh openpgp add manifest 4E1F0A2B7C9D8E6F5A4B3C2D1E0F9A8B7C6D5E4F /root/sb/.gnupg
\&./elebake.sh stage add smoke1
\&./elebake.sh stage sign key smoke1 pkcs11 db
\&./elebake.sh stage attest key smoke1 openpgp manifest
\&./elebake.sh stage checkout smoke1 platform\-trust\-gates\-15.1\(ha0 | sh
\&./elebake.sh stage make smoke1
\&./elebake.sh stage push smoke1 b
.EE
.PP
Take the database elsewhere \(en one signed pair, pinned on arrival:
.IP
.EX
\&./elebake.sh setenv ELEBAKE_ARCHIVE_ATTEST_KEY manifest
\&./elebake.sh export \(ti/git/config/dump.sh \(ti/.elebake/bundle/a1b2c3d.tar.gz full
# on the receiving machine
\&./elebake.sh openpgp add manifest 4E1F0A2B7C9D8E6F5A4B3C2D1E0F9A8B7C6D5E4F
\&./elebake.sh setenv ELEBAKE_ARCHIVE_ATTEST_KEY manifest
\&./elebake.sh import \(ti/git/config/dump.sh \(ti/.elebake/bundle/a1b2c3d.tar.gz
\&./elebake.sh provenance list
.EE
.PP
The rescue pair, and a rollback that keeps the evidence:
.IP
.EX
\&./elebake.sh export \(ti/rescue/dump.sh \(ti/rescue/bundle.tar.gz minimized
\&./elebake.sh stage backup list smoke1 a
\&./elebake.sh stage rollback smoke1 a known\-good\-p2
.EE
.PP
Inspect instead of act (any command): run it while the terminal default
is \f[CR]cat\f[R], read the emitted shell, then re\-run under an
executing pin.
